{
  "date": "2026-05-31",
  "period_start": "2026-05-01",
  "period_end": "2026-05-31",
  "title": "More models, one API",
  "summary": "May widened what builders can make through the API, while making app funding, integration, and community contributions easier to manage.\n\nEmbeddings gained an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, and the model catalog expanded across GPT, Gemini, Llama, Qwen, Claude, search, and video. Compatibility fixes made requests more predictable across providers.\n\nVideo gained reference images, start-and-end frames, and new model options; transcription gained speaker-labeled output. Realtime text-and-audio sessions arrived through a WebSocket API.\n\nBYOP app owners gained optional developer earnings and an earnings dashboard. Pollen added auto top-ups and local-currency checkout support, while accounting changes aligned recorded charges with the ledger.\n\nThe API docs gained focused BYOP, CLI, and MCP guides. React builders gained login hooks, account data, and themed UI components, with configurable key permissions and Pollen budgets.",
  "pr_count": 271,
